      ["ایک پلیٹ بریانی","ek pleṭ biryānī","a plate of biryani","No word for \"of\": the amount comes first, then the food."],
      ["ایک گلاس پانی","ek gilās pānī","a glass of water","Same pattern: ایک گلاس + the drink."],
      ["ایک میٹھی لسی","ek mīṭhī lassī","a sweet lassi","لسی is feminine, so میٹھی. Salty lassi is also common."],
      ["چینی نہ ڈالیں۔","chīnī na ḍālẽ.","No sugar, please.","نہ before a polite request means \"don't\". Chai usually comes sweet."],
      ["مجھے پیاس لگی ہے۔","mujhe pyās lagī hai.","I'm thirsty.","Literally \"thirst has struck me\": مجھے, not میں."],
      ["میں گوشت نہیں کھاتا۔","maĩ gosht nahī̃ khātā.","I don't eat meat. (a man speaking)","A woman says نہیں کھاتی. ہوں is often dropped after نہیں."],
      ["کھانا بہت مزیدار ہے۔","khānā bahut mazedār hai.","The food is delicious.","مزیدار never changes its ending."],
      ["آپ نے کھانا کھایا؟","āp ne khānā khāyā?","Have you eaten?","A friendly, caring question hosts and relatives ask all the time."],
      ["اور کچھ چاہیے؟","aur kuchh chāhie?","Anything else?","What a waiter or shopkeeper asks. Answer بس، شکریہ if you are done."],
      ["بس، شکریہ۔","bas, shukriyā.","That's all, thanks.","بس here means \"enough, that's it\"."]
